we've continually improved link ever  since we launched but sometimes change  can't be done incrementally sometimes  you have to clear the slate and start  again to achieve your vision and that is  what we've done with link to point 0  we've revamped major components of the  site to give it a clean fresh look and  to give the user a brand-new experience  learn is where you find lessons and  study them friends is where you interact  with members and tutors teach is where  you manage your tutoring activities and  tasks is where you find shortcuts to the  main activities on the site these four  simple controls are easy for newcomers  to learn and super efficient for power  users and that's just the start the new  learn page is like a control center for  link the timeline is a chronological  list of your learning activities and  site notifications want to find that  lesson you were just studying there it  is time to review that writing  correction or answer that conversation  request it's all right there in your  timeline on the other side of the page  you'll find recommendations these are  the courses or lessons that other  members are sharing as a lesson is  shared it moves to the top of the list  this gives you a constantly refreshing  list of lessons at your level that our  members are recommending as someone who  has learned to speak 12 languages  including five in the last 10 years I've  always felt that what mattered the most  to me was finding interesting material  to learn from that was at my level in  link to point 0 when you browse for  content new lessons open lessons  imported lessons they're all in one  place it's important to note that  courses replaces the old collections and  playlists replaces the old courses we  feel this terminology more accurately  reflects what these things do you can  view new lessons in the library lessons  you have already taken in my lessons or  lessons you have previously imported  select between lessons courses or  playlists depending on what you are  looking for  you can even filter your results further  when you find a lesson you like open it  if you really like it you may want to  add it to a playlist or share it with  others using the drop down menu  playlists are new to link winter  playlist playlist are a customized way  for you to collect lessons together to  suit a particular interest you have for  future study a lesson can belong to more  than one playlist you can even share  these playlists with other members to  help them maybe you're a tutor and want  to direct members learning your language  to some relevant content that you have  created or shared we think that  playlists will help everyone keep track  of good content and share it with others  to me it's about performance the site  has to work as efficiently and smoothly  as possible to allow people to focus on  what's important which is learning the  language ideally the technology the  system fades into the background what we  have done to the lesson page the core  page of our site is revolutionary we  fell in love with this new functionality  while testing and we've been waiting  impatiently for it to launch so we could  use it with our real account data the  new interface is much cleaner while at  the same time providing quicker access  to all functionality everything is  literally at your fingertips the text is  now fixed at an optimal width which  makes it easier to read as before new  words are highlighted in blue and links  the words you are learning in yellow on  the right in the dashboard pain you'll  find a new HTML audio player which works  well on all devices and platforms  including iOS devices you will also find  all information and resources related to  the lesson see the number of new words  and links in the lesson click to see the  new words or link terms drill down on a  term to see more information in the text  you'll notice that the word you're  looking up is bordered in red the  vocation of this word is now stored so  you can easily see where you are in the  lesson and find your way back if you  have to navigate away for some reason  like a bookmark but better but what  really gets us excited is the way you  can now quickly flip through these blue  new words just using your keyboard  the left/right arrow keys move you from  one new word to the next seamlessly and  the lesson text scrolls to keep up use  the up down arrow keys to choose the  best hint or option for the word and  enter to selectively there are also  options for ignore and known or you can  simply type X for ignore and k4 known we  wanted linking to be instant without a  lot of mousing the result is powerful  for vocabulary acquisition reviewing  links in the text is now just as easy as  dealing with your blue words just press  shift and the right or left arrow key to  switch from blue to yellow words now the  left and right arrow keys flip through  your links manage your tags view  examples see all user hints ask a tutor  for help review your notes while you  flip and while the text scrolls with you  all changes are automatically saved  lesson resources like videos  translations scripts and more are also  displayed in the dashboard red  indicators show which resources are  available just click to access a  specific resource from the drop-down  list more streamlined more functional  and fast we think you're going to love  it and if you're on a device with a  smaller resolution you can even minimize  the dashboard and use the full screen  for text highlighted words function as  they did in the original link app more  than two billion people have access to  the Internet to us that means amazing  opportunities to connect with learners  and speakers from all over the globe and  all this from your very own home as we  began this project of redoing link from  the ground up a core part of our vision  was enhancing the way that members  interact at link we knew from the start  that we had to make member interaction  more meaningful and more convenient in  order to create a truly vibrant learning  community the friends section features a  brand new activity wall front and center  now users can share updates links to  other sites videos images and more and  with privacy settings for each post you  can control what to share and more  importantly what to keep private you can  subscribe to specific users updates by  adding them as a friend giving you more  control over what you see in your feed  filter by less than  or conversations to see what your  friends are up to in your target  language of course part of the fun is in  the interaction and that's why we've  also added a comment box below each and  every post that appears allowing you to  comment on what other people have shared  if you like a post you can click the +  rose button to give it a rose if you  really like it you can even click the  share button and share it on your own  feed each time you click + rose on  someone's post a rose will be added to  the Rose total the sharing of lessons is  unique when you share a lesson you're  also giving it a rose this means that it  will be pushed to the top of the  recommendations list on the learn page  link to point 0 is not just an update  it's a genuine reinvention of the link  concept and a significant step forward  for language learners everywhere link is  now more portable more fun and more  effective the rest is up to you
 

